  "description": "Construction of a single storey rear outbuilding to be used ancillary to the main dwelling [Retrospective]",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The application has failed to demonstrate that the outbuilding will remain ancillary to the main dwelling. It provides the amenities for it to function as an independent residential unit, benefitting from access routes independent from the host dwelling. It fails to reflect the surrounding context and would compromise the character of the area. The proposal represents an&nbsp;inappropriate and uncharacteristic residential form in a rear garden setting&nbsp;which results in harm to the character and context of the area.&nbsp; As such, the proposal is contrary to:&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023)Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021);The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012);Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan: (September 2024)&nbsp;"
  ],
